IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: THE SCHEDULES (Schedule 1 transitional and savings; Schedule 2 incorporation by reference; the opening rule of Schedule 3).
-- The Act dates none of the commencement dates it names ("the main commencement date" is the day section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force, and so on): each is a DATE input.
-- "Anniversary" is not defined (no rule for 29 February, or for what a year is, see nz-interpretation-time.l4): each anniversary the Act mentions is a DATE input.
-- Schedule 1 clauses 1, 11 and 12 (overview, purpose, outline) create no rule; clause 19 (the transitional regulation-making power, apart from subclauses (5) and (6)) and clause 35 (saving for an existing appointment) are machinery; clauses 30 and 31, Schedule 1A and Schedule 4 are blank in the text: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- The Schedule 3 tables reach the deposited text without their empowering-provision cells (see NOTES.md, finding on Schedule 3), so the schedule is one rule whose match against the tables is an input.

§ `Schedule 1 clause 2 -- Definitions for this Part`

-- src:1045 | main commencement date means the date on which section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 (which repeals the Legislation Act 2012) comes into force
-- src:1041 | 2 Definitions for this Part
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 2, definition of main commencement date (src:1041) (src:1045)
GIVEN `the day section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the main commencement date` `the day section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force` MEANS
    `the day section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force`

-- src:1046 | publication commencement date means the date on which section 17 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force (which brings into force the amendments requiring centralised publication as set out in Schedule 2 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 2, definition of publication commencement date (src:1046)
GIVEN `the day section 17 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the publication commencement date` `the day section 17 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force` MEANS
    `the day section 17 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 comes into force`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 3 -- Part 2 of this Act applies to both existing and new legislation`

-- src:1053 | Part 2 of this Act applies to—
-- src:1054 | legislation whether it is enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date; and
-- src:1055 | anything that was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made (or an amendment to that enactment made at any time).
-- Part 2 applies to legislation whether it is enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date; and to anything that was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made (or an amendment to that enactment made at any time).
-- src:1052 | 3 Part 2 of this Act applies to both existing and new legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 3 (src:1052) (src:1053-1055)
GIVEN `it is legislation, whether enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Part 2 applies to the legislation or enactment` `it is legislation, whether enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date` `it was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made` MEANS
    `it is legislation, whether enacted or made before, on, or after the main commencement date` OR `it was an enactment under the Interpretation Act 1999 at the time it was made`

-- (2) This clause is subject to the rest of this subpart: where another provision of the subpart says otherwise, that provision prevails over clause 3.
-- src:1056 | This clause is subject to the rest of this subpart.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 3(2) (src:1056)
GIVEN `another provision of the rest of subpart 1 says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 3 applies` `another provision of the rest of subpart 1 says otherwise` MEANS
    (NOT `another provision of the rest of subpart 1 says otherwise`)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 4 -- Exception for examples in existing legislation`

-- src:1057 | 4 Exception for examples in existing legislation
-- src:1058 | Section 23 does not apply to an example provided in legislation that is enacted or made before the main commencement date (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation).
-- src:1059 | This clause applies unless—
-- src:1060 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1061 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
-- Section 23 does not apply to an example provided in legislation that is enacted or made before the main commencement date (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation). This applies unless the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation.
-- So section 23 applies to every other example, and to these when the legislation provides otherwise or the context requires it. Section 23 itself is in nz-part2-definitions.l4.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 4 (src:1057) (src:1058-1061)
GIVEN `the day the legislation containing the example was enacted or made` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the example is in an amendment made after that date to that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` `the day the legislation containing the example was enacted or made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `where it is in a later amendment:` `the example is in an amendment made after that date to that legislation` `and the legislation provides otherwise:` `the legislation provides otherwise` `or the context requires:` `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation` MEANS
    NOT (    ((`the day the legislation containing the example was enacted or made` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`) OR `the example is in an amendment made after that date to that legislation`)
         AND (NOT (`the legislation provides otherwise` OR `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation`)))

§ `Schedule 1 clause 5 -- Exception for commencement of secondary legislation made before main commencement date`

-- src:1062 | 5 Exception for commencement of secondary legislation made before main commencement date
-- src:1063 | Section 26 does not apply to secondary legislation made before the main commencement date (and section 9 of the Interpretation Act 1999 applies instead).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 5 (src:1062) (src:1063)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 26 applies to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` MEANS
    NOT (`the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 6 -- Saving of definitions for pre-1 November 1999 legislation`

DECLARE `Term saved by clause 6` IS ONE OF
    Act
    Governor
    land
    person
    `another term`

-- src:1065 | 6 Saving of definitions for pre-1 November 1999 legislation
-- src:1066 | In legislation enacted or made before 1 November 1999 (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation),—
-- src:1067 | Act includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act
-- src:1068 | Governor means the Governor-General
-- src:1069 | land includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure
-- src:1070 | person includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate.
-- src:1071 | This clause applies to legislation unless—
-- src:1072 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1073 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
-- In legislation enacted or made before 1 November 1999 (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation), the four terms have the old meanings, unless the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 6 (src:1065) (src:1066-1073)
GIVEN term IS A `Term saved by clause 6`
      `the day the legislation was enacted or made` IS A DATE
      `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the saved meaning of the term` term `in legislation enacted or made on` `the day the legislation was enacted or made` `when it is a later amendment:` `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation` `and it is displaced:` `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation` MEANS
    IF (    ((`the day the legislation was enacted or made` LESS THAN (Date 1 11 1999)) OR `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation`)
        AND (NOT `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation`))
    THEN CONSIDER term
         WHEN Act THEN JUST "includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act"
         WHEN Governor THEN JUST "means the Governor-General"
         WHEN land THEN JUST "includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure"
         WHEN person THEN JUST "includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate"
         WHEN `another term` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- What each saved definition of clause 6 covers. "Act includes", "land includes" and "person includes" are OPEN lists (a candidate off the list is neither in nor out, NOTHING); "Governor means" is CLOSED (anyone but the Governor-General is JUST FALSE).
-- "Houses and buildings" are land unless there are words to exclude them.
DECLARE `Candidate within a term saved by clause 6` IS ONE OF
    `rules made under the Act`
    `regulations made under the Act`
    `the Governor-General`
    `someone other than the Governor-General`
    `messuages`
    `tenements`
    `hereditaments`
    `houses`
    `buildings`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a body of persons that is corporate`
    `a body of persons that is unincorporate`
    `something else`

-- src:1067 | Act includes rules and regulations (within the meaning of those terms as used in the Acts Interpretation Act 1924) made under the Act
-- src:1068 | Governor means the Governor-General
-- src:1069 | land includes messuages, tenements, hereditaments, houses, and buildings unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure
-- src:1070 | person includes a corporation sole, and also a body of persons, whether corporate or unincorporate.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 6 (src:1067-1070)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate within a term saved by clause 6`
      `there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is within the saved meaning of the pre-1 November 1999 term` candidate `unless there are words to exclude houses and buildings:` `there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure` MEANS
    CONSIDER candidate
    WHEN `rules made under the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `regulations made under the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Governor-General` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone other than the Governor-General` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `messuages` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `tenements` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `hereditaments` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `houses` THEN JUST (NOT `there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure`)
    WHEN `buildings` THEN JUST (NOT `there are words to exclude houses and buildings, or to restrict the meaning to tenements of some particular tenure`)
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body of persons that is corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body of persons that is unincorporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

§ `Schedule 1 clause 7 -- Saving of definitions for legislation made before main commencement date`

-- src:1074 | 7 Saving of definitions for legislation made before main commencement date
-- src:1075 | In legislation enacted or made before the main commencement date (or an amendment, after that date, to that legislation), regulations has the meaning set out in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 (as in force immediately before that date).
-- src:1076 | This clause applies to legislation unless—
-- src:1077 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:1078 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 7 (src:1074) (src:1075-1078)
GIVEN `the day the legislation was enacted or made` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
      `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulations has the meaning in section 29 of the Interpretation Act 1999 for legislation enacted or made on` `the day the legislation was enacted or made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `when it is a later amendment:` `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation` `and it is displaced:` `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation` MEANS
        ((`the day the legislation was enacted or made` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`) OR `it is an amendment made after that date to that legislation`)
    AND (NOT `the legislation provides otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation`)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 8 -- Savings of previous Proclamations`

-- src:1079 | 8 Savings of previous Proclamations
-- src:1080 | A Proclamation published in the Gazette before the main commencement date continues to be a proclamation for the purposes of section 13.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 8 (src:1079) (src:1080)
GIVEN `it is a Proclamation published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was published` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a previous Proclamation continues to be a proclamation for section 13` `it is a Proclamation published in the Gazette` `the day it was published` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` MEANS
    `it is a Proclamation published in the Gazette` AND (`the day it was published` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 9 -- Savings of material incorporated by reference under Legislation Act 2012`

-- src:1082 | Material incorporated by reference under subpart 2 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 must be treated as if—
-- src:1083 | it were incorporated by reference under section 64 of this Act; and
-- src:1084 | any notice given under section 52(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 as to where the material is available for inspection and purchase is public notice as to where it is publicly available for the purposes of clause 2(a) of Schedule 2 of this Act.
-- src:1081 | 9 Savings of material incorporated by reference under Legislation Act 2012
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 9(1) (src:1081) (src:1082-1084)
GIVEN `it was incorporated by reference under subpart 2 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the material is treated as incorporated by reference under section 64` `it was incorporated by reference under subpart 2 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012` MEANS
    `it was incorporated by reference under subpart 2 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012`

@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 9(1)(b) (src:1084)
GIVEN `the notice was given under section 52(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 as to where the material is available for inspection and purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the old notice is public notice of where the material is publicly available` `the notice was given under section 52(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 as to where the material is available for inspection and purchase` MEANS
    `the notice was given under section 52(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 as to where the material is available for inspection and purchase`

-- src:1085 | The chief executive may make it publicly available in another way permitted by Schedule 2 of this Act if the chief executive gives public notice as required by clause 2 of that schedule.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 9(2) (src:1085)
GIVEN `the chief executive gives public notice as required by clause 2 of Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chief executive may make the material publicly available in another way permitted by Schedule 2` `the chief executive gives public notice as required by clause 2 of Schedule 2` MEANS
    `the chief executive gives public notice as required by clause 2 of Schedule 2`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 10 -- How Abolition of Provinces Act 1875 affects provincial legislation`

-- src:1086 | 10 How Abolition of Provinces Act 1875 affects provincial legislation
-- src:1087 | Section 26 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1908 as set out in Schedule 2 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1924 continues to apply despite its repeal.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 10 (src:1086) (src:1087)
GIVEN `the section is section 26 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1908 as set out in Schedule 2 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1924` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section continues to apply despite its repeal` `the section is section 26 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1908 as set out in Schedule 2 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1924` MEANS
    `the section is section 26 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1908 as set out in Schedule 2 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1924`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 13 -- Definition of secondary legislation is effective on main commencement date for all legislation`

-- src:1116 | An instrument made before that date that is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision, becomes, on the main commencement date, secondary legislation.
-- (2) An instrument made before the main commencement date that is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision becomes, on the main commencement date, secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 13(2) (src:1116)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was made` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
      `it is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an instrument made on` `the day the instrument was made` `becomes secondary legislation, given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `when` `it is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision` MEANS
    IF (`the day the instrument was made` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`) AND `it is in force under a provision that empowers the making of secondary legislation, under the Royal prerogative, or under an identified empowering provision`
    THEN JUST `the main commencement date`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) A provision is an identified empowering provision if an amendment to the legislation (a secondary legislation amendment) has been passed or made that will result in the legislation stating that instruments under that provision are secondary legislation, but that amendment is not yet in force.
-- src:1128 | For the purposes of this Act, a provision is an identified empowering provision if an amendment to the legislation (a secondary legislation amendment)—
-- src:1130 | that amendment is not yet in force.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 13(3) (src:1128-1130)
GIVEN `a secondary legislation amendment has been passed or made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that amendment is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an identified empowering provision` `a secondary legislation amendment has been passed or made` `that amendment is in force` MEANS
    `a secondary legislation amendment has been passed or made` AND (NOT `that amendment is in force`)

-- (1) The definition applies to an instrument regardless of whether it is made before, on, or after the main commencement date, and extends to an instrument made under an identified empowering provision.
-- src:1113 | The definition of secondary legislation—
-- src:1115 | extends to an instrument made under an identified empowering provision (see subclause (3)).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 13(1) (src:1113-1115)
GIVEN `the instrument meets the definition of secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made under an identified empowering provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is secondary legislation under clause 13` `the instrument meets the definition of secondary legislation` `the instrument is made under an identified empowering provision` MEANS
    `the instrument meets the definition of secondary legislation` OR `the instrument is made under an identified empowering provision`

-- (5) Subpart 2 of Part 3 applies to the changes the Chief Parliamentary Counsel authorises under (4) as if they were changes referred to in section 87, except that (a) those changes must be treated as being revoked immediately before the secondary legislation amendments come into force;
-- and (b) section 90 (which deals with when editorial changes usually take effect) does not apply.
-- src:1135 | Subpart 2 of Part 3 applies to those changes as if they were changes referred to in section 87, except that, for the purposes of ensuring that the secondary legislation amendments (and any other related amendments relating to listing, notification, publication, or presentation) are effective despite those changes,—
-- src:1137 | section 90 (which deals with when editorial changes usually take effect) does not apply.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 13(5) (src:1135-1137)
GIVEN `the change is one authorised under clause 13(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 90 applies to the change` `the change is one authorised under clause 13(4)` MEANS
    NOT `the change is one authorised under clause 13(4)`

-- The printed item (b) names four subjects of statement: listing, notification, publication, presentation (ruling C).
DECLARE `Change to a version of legislation under clause 13(4)` IS ONE OF
    `inserting a statement to make it clear that instruments made under identified empowering provisions are secondary legislation`
    `inserting, replacing or removing a statement relating to listing, notification, publication or presentation`
    `inserting, replacing or removing a statement relating to listing`
    `inserting, replacing or removing a statement relating to notification`
    `inserting, replacing or removing a statement relating to publication`
    `inserting, replacing or removing a statement relating to presentation`
    `a change purely consequential on those changes`
    `another change`

-- (4) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make the following changes to a version of legislation, to show the effect of subclauses (1)(b) and (3), the rest of this schedule, and Part 3 in relation to identified empowering provisions: (a) statements that
-- instruments made under identified empowering provisions are secondary legislation; (b) statements relating to listing, notification, publication or presentation; (c) any other changes purely consequential on those. A change of another kind is not mentioned here.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): "the following changes" is a closed list of grants by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel's authority, so a change of another kind is not given by this subclause: JUST FALSE.
-- src:1131 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make the following changes to a version of legislation to show the effect of subclauses (1)﻿(b) and (3), the rest of this schedule, and Part 3 in relation to identified empowering provisions:
-- src:1134 | any other changes that are purely consequential on those changes.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 13(4) (src:1131-1134)
GIVEN change IS A `Change to a version of legislation under clause 13(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make the change` change MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `another change` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 14 -- Existing requirements continued as applicable publication requirements on main commencement date`

-- src:1139 | This clause applies, for the purposes of section 74(1)﻿(a), to empowering provisions that are enacted before the main commencement date.
-- src:1140 | For the purposes of the applicable publication requirements under that paragraph (as in force on the main commencement date),—
-- src:1141 | the PCO may record and publish, as the applicable publication requirements for the empowering provision,—
-- src:1142 | the 1 or more requirements to publish, notify, or otherwise make available secondary legislation made under the empowering provision that applied under an Act, with the same or substantially the same effect, immediately before the main commencement date; and with
-- src:1143 | any exemptions or limits on those requirements; and with
-- src:1144 | any necessary modifications in light of other amendments made to the legislation on or after the main commencement date; and
-- src:1138 | 14 Existing requirements continued as applicable publication requirements on main commencement date
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 14(1) and (2)(a) (src:1138) (src:1139-1144)
GIVEN `the empowering provision was enacted before the main commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO may record and publish the earlier requirements as the applicable publication requirements` `the empowering provision was enacted before the main commencement date` MEANS
    `the empowering provision was enacted before the main commencement date`

-- src:1145 | the PCO must publish those applicable publication requirements, on the legislation website, by publishing either a link to the previous provision that set out that requirement or the record made under paragraph (a).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 14(2)(b) (src:1145)
GIVEN `the PCO has recorded the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PCO publishes a link to the previous provision or the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO has published the applicable publication requirements as clause 14 requires` `the PCO has recorded the requirements` `the PCO publishes a link to the previous provision or the record` MEANS
    `the PCO has recorded the requirements` AND `the PCO publishes a link to the previous provision or the record`

-- (3) Nothing in clause 14 limits the information that the PCO may record and publish in relation to an Act in relation to an empowering provision.
-- src:1146 | Nothing in this clause limits the information that the PCO may record and publish in relation to an Act in relation to an empowering provision (for example, as an aid to assist users to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 14(3) (src:1146)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 14 limits the information that the PCO may record and publish in relation to an empowering provision` MEANS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 15 -- Maker must lodge minimum legislative information before list deadline (if clause applies)`

-- src:1148 | This clause applies to secondary legislation on and after the publication commencement date if—
-- src:1149 | it is made before the list deadline; and
-- src:1150 | it is not already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before that list deadline.
-- (1) This clause applies to secondary legislation on and after the publication commencement date if it is made before the list deadline and it is not already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before that list deadline.
-- src:1147 | 15 Maker must lodge minimum legislative information before list deadline (if clause applies)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(1) (src:1147) (src:1148-1150)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the list deadline` IS A DATE
      `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the list deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 15 applies on` `the day asked about` `to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `when the publication commencement date is` `the publication commencement date` `and the list deadline is` `the list deadline` `and it is already required to be published:` `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the list deadline` MEANS
        (`the day asked about` AT LEAST `the publication commencement date`)
    AND (`the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN `the list deadline`)
    AND (NOT `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the list deadline`)

-- (2) Until the list deadline a list exemption applies. "Until" includes the deadline day (nz-interpretation-time.l4, s 54 Item 5). (3) The maker must, before the list deadline, lodge the minimum legislative information: the last day for lodging is the day before the deadline (Item 6).
-- src:1152 | a list exemption applies to the secondary legislation; and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(2)(a) (src:1152)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the list deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a list exemption applies on` `the day asked about` `when the list deadline is` `the list deadline` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT MOST `the list deadline`

-- src:1157 | The maker must, before the list deadline, lodge the minimum legislative information for the secondary legislation with the PCO for publication in accordance with the regulations (unless the secondary legislation ceases to be in force before the list deadline).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(3) (src:1157)
GIVEN `the day the minimum legislative information is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the list deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the minimum legislative information is lodged in time on` `the day the minimum legislative information is lodged` `when the list deadline is` `the list deadline` MEANS
    `the day the minimum legislative information is lodged` LESS THAN `the list deadline`

-- (2)(b) The applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied if the minimum legislative information is, with the agreement of the PCO, instead lodged with the PCO for publication, and the maker complies with the minimum requirements for publication set by regulations (if any).
-- src:1153 | the maker must continue to comply with the applicable publication requirements (to the extent required by section 73, as in force immediately before the publication commencement date); but
-- src:1156 | the maker complies with the minimum requirements for publication set by regulations made under this Act that are applicable (if any).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(2)(b) (src:1153-1156)
GIVEN `the minimum legislative information is lodged with the PCO, with the agreement of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker complies with the applicable minimum requirements set by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicable publication requirements are treated as satisfied until the list deadline` `the minimum legislative information is lodged with the PCO, with the agreement of the PCO` `the maker complies with the applicable minimum requirements set by regulations` MEANS
    `the minimum legislative information is lodged with the PCO, with the agreement of the PCO` AND `the maker complies with the applicable minimum requirements set by regulations`

-- (4) The secondary legislation is revoked on a date specified in the regulations if its minimum legislative information is not lodged with the PCO for publication, and it is of a class specified by the regulations as being revoked on that date.
-- src:1158 | The secondary legislation is revoked on a date specified in the regulations if—
-- src:1160 | it is of a class that is specified by the regulations as being revoked on that date.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(4) (src:1158-1160)
GIVEN `its minimum legislative information is not lodged with the PCO for publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the secondary legislation is revoked for want of minimum legislative information` `its minimum legislative information is not lodged with the PCO for publication` `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date` `the date specified in the regulations` MEANS
    IF `its minimum legislative information is not lodged with the PCO for publication` AND `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date`
    THEN JUST `the date specified in the regulations`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5) The list deadline is (a) the first anniversary of the publication commencement date (unless (b) or (c) applies); or (b) a deadline after the publication commencement date and no later than the fifth anniversary that is set by the regulations for the relevant class;
-- or (c) a deadline earlier than a deadline under (a) or (b) that is set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel. The anniversaries are supplied (the Act does not define them). A regulations deadline outside the range in (b) is not a (b) deadline: the text does not say what then applies.
-- src:1161 | The list deadline for secondary legislation is—
-- src:1164 | a deadline earlier than a deadline under paragraph (a) or (b) that is set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(5) (src:1161-1164)
GIVEN `the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the first anniversary of the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the deadline set by the regulations for the class` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the list deadline given the publication commencement date` `the publication commencement date` `and the first anniversary` `the first anniversary of the publication commencement date` `and the fifth anniversary` `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date` `and the regulations' deadline` `the deadline set by the regulations for the class` `and the agreed deadline` `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the deadline set by the regulations for the class`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the earlier of a deadline and an agreed deadline` `the first anniversary of the publication commencement date` `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`
    WHEN JUST fromRegulations THEN
        IF (fromRegulations GREATER THAN `the publication commencement date`) AND (fromRegulations AT MOST `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date`)
        THEN `the earlier of a deadline and an agreed deadline` fromRegulations `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- Helper for (5)(c): an agreed deadline counts only if it is earlier than the deadline under (a) or (b).
GIVEN deadline IS A DATE
      agreed IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earlier of a deadline and an agreed deadline` deadline agreed MEANS
    CONSIDER agreed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST deadline
    WHEN JUST agreedDay THEN IF agreedDay LESS THAN deadline THEN JUST agreedDay ELSE JUST deadline

-- The printed items name several things: sections 75, 76 and 77; directions under section 76, 36E or 36F (ruling C).
DECLARE `Thing that continues` IS ONE OF
    `sections 75 to 77 (as in force immediately before the publication commencement date)`
    `section 75 (as in force immediately before the publication commencement date)`
    `section 76 (as in force immediately before the publication commencement date)`
    `section 77 (as in force immediately before the publication commencement date)`
    `any direction made under section 76 (or previously under section 36E or 36F of the Legislation Act 2012)`
    `any direction made under section 76`
    `any direction made previously under section 36E of the Legislation Act 2012`
    `any direction made previously under section 36F of the Legislation Act 2012`
    `any regulations made for the purposes of the definition of relevant central government entity`
    `anything else`

-- (6) For secondary legislation with international transparency obligations: sections 75 to 77 continue to apply (as in force immediately before the publication commencement date); any direction under section 76 continues in force, and may continue to be amended or revoked;
-- any regulations made for the definition of relevant central government entity continue in force, and may continue to be amended or revoked.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): subclause (6) is a closed list of what continues, so anything else is not continued by it: JUST FALSE.
-- src:1165 | For the purposes of subclause (2)﻿(b), in relation to the applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation with international transparency obligations,—
-- src:1168 | any regulations made for the purposes of the definition of relevant central government entity continue in force, and may continue to be amended or revoked as if section 147(1)﻿(d) were still in force.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 15(6) (src:1165-1168)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that continues`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`for secondary legislation with international transparency obligations this continues` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `anything else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 16 -- Maker must lodge secondary legislation for full publication before publication deadline (if clause applies)`

-- src:1170 | This clause applies to secondary legislation on and after the publication commencement date if—
-- src:1171 | it is made before the publication deadline; and
-- src:1172 | it is not already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before that publication deadline.
-- src:1169 | 16 Maker must lodge secondary legislation for full publication before publication deadline (if clause applies)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 16(1) (src:1169) (src:1170-1172)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the publication deadline` IS A DATE
      `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the publication deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 16 applies on` `the day asked about` `to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `when the publication commencement date is` `the publication commencement date` `and the publication deadline is` `the publication deadline` `and it is already required to be published:` `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the publication deadline` MEANS
        (`the day asked about` AT LEAST `the publication commencement date`)
    AND (`the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN `the publication deadline`)
    AND (NOT `it is already required to be published by the PCO under Part 3 before the publication deadline`)

-- src:1173 | A publication exemption applies to the secondary legislation until the publication deadline (see section 76, as in force on the publication commencement date, for the publication obligations that instead apply).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 16(2) (src:1173)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the publication deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a publication exemption applies on` `the day asked about` `when the publication deadline is` `the publication deadline` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT MOST `the publication deadline`

-- src:1174 | The maker must, before the publication deadline, lodge the secondary legislation with the PCO for publication in accordance with the regulations (unless the secondary legislation ceases to be in force before the publication deadline).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 16(3) (src:1174)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the publication deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the secondary legislation is lodged in time on` `the day the secondary legislation is lodged` `when the publication deadline is` `the publication deadline` MEANS
    `the day the secondary legislation is lodged` LESS THAN `the publication deadline`

-- src:1175 | The secondary legislation is revoked on a date specified in the regulations if—
-- src:1177 | it is of a class that is specified by the regulations as being revoked on that date.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 16(4) (src:1175-1177)
GIVEN `it is not lodged with the PCO for publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the secondary legislation is revoked for want of lodgement` `it is not lodged with the PCO for publication` `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date` `the date specified in the regulations` MEANS
    IF `it is not lodged with the PCO for publication` AND `it is of a class that the regulations specify as being revoked on that date`
    THEN JUST `the date specified in the regulations`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5) The publication deadline is (a) a deadline set by the regulations for the relevant class; or (b) an earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel. Without a regulations deadline the text gives none.
-- src:1178 | The publication deadline for secondary legislation is—
-- src:1180 | an earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 16(5) (src:1178-1180)
GIVEN `the deadline set by the regulations for the class` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the publication deadline given the regulations' deadline` `the deadline set by the regulations for the class` `and the agreed deadline` `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the deadline set by the regulations for the class`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fromRegulations THEN `the earlier of a deadline and an agreed deadline` fromRegulations `the earlier deadline set by agreement between the maker and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 17 and 18 -- Publication of information lodged under this subpart; application of subpart 1 of Part 3`

-- src:1181 | 17 Publication of information and secondary legislation to which this subpart applies
-- src:1182 | The PCO must publish the minimum legislative information, and the secondary legislation, that is lodged under this subpart when required to do so by the regulations (but need not do so before that time).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 17 (src:1181) (src:1182)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the regulations require the PCO to publish` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must publish lodged information on` `the day asked about` `when the regulations require publication on` `the day the regulations require the PCO to publish` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day the regulations require the PCO to publish`

DECLARE `Section of subpart 1 of Part 3` IS ONE OF
    `section 71`
    `section 73`
    `another section specified in the regulations`
    `any other section of subpart 1 of Part 3`

-- src:1183 | 18 Application of subpart 1 of Part 3 of this Act
-- src:1184 | The following sections do not apply to minimum legislative information lodged, or required to be lodged, under clause 15 or secondary legislation lodged, or required to be lodged, under clause 16 (except as provided in the regulations):
-- src:1185 | section 71 (how and when PCO must publish legislation and consolidations of legislation):
-- src:1186 | section 73 (secondary legislation does not commence until published):
-- src:1187 | any other sections of subpart 1 of Part 3 of this Act that are specified in the regulations.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 18 (src:1183) (src:1184-1187)
GIVEN section IS A `Section of subpart 1 of Part 3`
      `the regulations provide that it applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the section applies to information lodged under clause 15 or legislation lodged under clause 16` section `when` `the regulations provide that it applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `any other section of subpart 1 of Part 3` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `the regulations provide that it applies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clause 19 -- Transitional regulation-making power`

-- src:1205 | Regulations made under this clause are secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
-- (5) Regulations made under this clause are secondary legislation. (6) This clause is repealed on the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date: repealed at the start of that day (section 39), so in force through the day before.
-- src:1189 | 19 Transitional regulation-making power
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 19(5) (src:1189) (src:1205)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulations made under clause 19 are secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1206 | This clause is repealed on the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 19(6) (src:1206)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 19 is still in force on` `the day asked about` `when the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date is` `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date` MEANS
    `legislation expressed to be repealed on` `the fifth anniversary of the publication commencement date` `is still in force on` `the day asked about`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 20 -- Transitional application of publication responsibilities`

DECLARE `Thing the PCO might have to publish` IS ONE OF
    `a Bill (or amendments to it)`
    `an Act`
    `secondary legislation`
    `minimum legislative information for secondary legislation`

-- src:1208 | Section 69, and other publication or notification responsibilities for the PCO under Part 3 (as in force on the main commencement date), do not apply to—
-- src:1209 | Bills that were introduced before 5 August 2013 (or amendments to those Bills):
-- src:1210 | Acts that ceased to be in force before 5 August 2013:
-- src:1211 | secondary legislation that ceases to be in force before 5 August 2013:
-- src:1212 | minimum legislative information for that secondary legislation.
-- (1) Section 69, and other publication or notification responsibilities of the PCO under Part 3 (as in force on the main commencement date), do not apply to Bills introduced before 5 August 2013 (or amendments to them), Acts that ceased to be in force before 5 August 2013,
-- secondary legislation that ceases to be in force before 5 August 2013, and its minimum legislative information. The thing's date is: the day the Bill was introduced; the day the Act or secondary legislation ceased to be in force.
-- src:1207 | 20 Transitional application of publication responsibilities
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 20(1) (src:1207) (src:1208-1212)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing the PCO might have to publish`
      `its date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO's responsibilities do not apply before 5 August 2013 to` thing `with date` `its date` MEANS
    `its date` LESS THAN (Date 5 8 2013)

-- (2) From the publication commencement date the responsibilities also do not apply to secondary legislation that ceases to be in force before the list deadline (and was not required to be published by the PCO before that date), or its minimum legislative information.
-- src:1213 | Section 69, and other publication responsibilities for the PCO under Part 3 (as in force on and from the publication commencement date), continue to not apply to the things set out in subclause (1), but also do not apply to—
-- src:1215 | minimum legislative information for that secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 20(2) (src:1213-1215)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation ceases to be in force` IS A DATE
      `the list deadline` IS A DATE
      `it was required to be published by the PCO before the list deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO's responsibilities also do not apply to secondary legislation that ceased to be in force on` `the day the secondary legislation ceases to be in force` `before the list deadline` `the list deadline` `when it was required to be published:` `it was required to be published by the PCO before the list deadline` MEANS
    (`the day the secondary legislation ceases to be in force` LESS THAN `the list deadline`) AND (NOT `it was required to be published by the PCO before the list deadline`)

-- (3) Sections 75 to 77 (as in force on the main commencement date) do not apply to secondary legislation made before 30 December 2018. (4) Section 73 (as inserted by Schedule 2 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019) does not apply to any secondary legislation made before that section comes into force.
-- src:1216 | Sections 75 to 77 (as in force on the main commencement date) do not apply to secondary legislation made before 30 December 2018.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 20(3) (src:1216)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sections 75 to 77 as in force on the main commencement date apply to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` MEANS
    NOT (`the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN (Date 30 12 2018))

-- src:1217 | Section 73 (as inserted by Schedule 2 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019) does not apply to any secondary legislation that is made before that section comes into force.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 20(4) (src:1217)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the day section 73 as inserted comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 73 as inserted applies to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `when section 73 as inserted comes into force on` `the day section 73 as inserted comes into force` MEANS
    NOT (`the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN `the day section 73 as inserted comes into force`)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 21 -- Power to reassign responsibilities of secondary legislation's maker`

-- src:1220 | An authorisation is made by written notice given to the department and, unless the department is the PCO, copied to the PCO.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 21(2) (src:1220)
GIVEN `written notice is given to the department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is given to the PCO, or the department is the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General's authorisation is made` `written notice is given to the department` `a copy is given to the PCO, or the department is the PCO` MEANS
    `written notice is given to the department` AND `a copy is given to the PCO, or the department is the PCO`

-- (3) An authorisation expires on the publication deadline: "expires" is a kind of repeal (section 13), so it ends at the start of that day (section 39).
-- src:1221 | Any authorisation under this section expires on the publication deadline set for that secondary legislation under the regulations.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 21(3) (src:1221)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the publication deadline` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authorisation is still in force on` `the day asked about` `when the publication deadline is` `the publication deadline` MEANS
    `legislation expressed to be repealed on` `the publication deadline` `is still in force on` `the day asked about`

-- (1) The Attorney-General may authorise any department (within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Public Finance Act 1989) to meet, in relation to secondary legislation, an obligation under this Act that would otherwise have to be met by the legislation's maker under this schedule.
-- Whether the body is a department within the meaning of that Act is a fact borrowed from another Act and is asked as an input.
-- src:1219 | The Attorney-General may authorise any department (within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Public Finance Act 1989) to meet, in relation to secondary legislation, an obligation under this Act that would otherwise have to be met by the legislation’s maker under this schedule.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 21(1) (src:1219)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a department within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Public Finance Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is one the maker would otherwise have to meet under this schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the department may meet the maker's obligation in the maker's place` `the Attorney-General has authorised it` `it is a department within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Public Finance Act 1989` `the obligation is one the maker would otherwise have to meet under this schedule` MEANS
    `the Attorney-General has authorised it` AND `it is a department within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Public Finance Act 1989` AND `the obligation is one the maker would otherwise have to meet under this schedule`

§ `Schedule 1 clause 22 -- Commencement orders for existing Acts are secondary legislation`

-- src:1222 | 22 Commencement orders for existing Acts are secondary legislation
-- src:1223 | This clause applies to an Act’s commencement provision if—
-- src:1224 | the Act is enacted before the main commencement date; and
-- src:1225 | the provision provides for all or part of the Act to be brought into force by Order in Council; and
-- src:1226 | the commencement provision does not state that a commencement order under the provision is secondary legislation.
-- src:1227 | A commencement order made under the provision is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 22 (src:1222) (src:1223-1227)
GIVEN `the Act was enacted before the main commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision provides for all or part of the Act to be brought into force by Order in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commencement provision states that a commencement order under it is secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a commencement order under the provision is secondary legislation by clause 22` `the Act was enacted before the main commencement date` `the provision provides for all or part of the Act to be brought into force by Order in Council` `the commencement provision states that a commencement order under it is secondary legislation` MEANS
    `the Act was enacted before the main commencement date`
    AND `the provision provides for all or part of the Act to be brought into force by Order in Council`
    AND (NOT `the commencement provision states that a commencement order under it is secondary legislation`)

§ `Schedule 1 clauses 23 and 24 -- Drafting responsibilities`

-- src:1231 | This clause applies to secondary legislation made under an empowering provision if, immediately before the main commencement date, section 59(2)﻿(c) or (d) of the Legislation Act 2012 required the PCO to draft instruments made under that empowering provision.
-- src:1232 | The administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel are assumed to have agreed, for the purpose of section 67(d) of this Act, that the PCO will draft secondary legislation made under the provision.
-- src:1233 | Subclause (2) applies only until either party notifies the other that they do not agree or the parties reach a different agreement under section 67(d).
-- src:1234 | This clause does not apply to secondary legislation to which section 59(2)﻿(a) or (b) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied.
-- src:1230 | 23 PCO’s responsibility for drafting secondary legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 23 (src:1230) (src:1231-1234)
GIVEN `section 59(2)(c) or (d) of the Legislation Act 2012 required the PCO to draft instruments under the empowering provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 59(2)(a) or (b) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied to the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either party has notified the other that they do not agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have reached a different agreement under section 67(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel are assumed to have agreed that the PCO will draft` `section 59(2)(c) or (d) of the Legislation Act 2012 required the PCO to draft instruments under the empowering provision` `section 59(2)(a) or (b) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied to the secondary legislation` `either party has notified the other that they do not agree` `the parties have reached a different agreement under section 67(d)` MEANS
        `section 59(2)(c) or (d) of the Legislation Act 2012 required the PCO to draft instruments under the empowering provision`
    AND (NOT `section 59(2)(a) or (b) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied to the secondary legislation`)
    AND (NOT `either party has notified the other that they do not agree`)
    AND (NOT `the parties have reached a different agreement under section 67(d)`)

-- Clause 24: the PCO may continue to draft and publish any instrument described in section 59(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 until the administering agency or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel notifies the other of an end date. "Until" includes the end date (Item 5).
-- src:1236 | The PCO may, after the main commencement date, continue to draft and publish any instrument described in section 59(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 until the administering agency or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel notifies the other of an end date for the purposes of this clause.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 24 (src:1236)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the end date notified` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO may continue to draft and publish instruments described in section 59(2) of the Legislation Act 2012 on` `the day asked about` `given the end date notified` `the end date notified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end date notified`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST endDay THEN `the day asked about` AT MOST endDay

§ `Schedule 1 clauses 25 to 29 -- Official versions, editorial changes and revision Bills`

-- src:1239 | Section 78 applies to legislation regardless of when it is or was made, printed, or published.
-- src:1240 | An official electronic version of legislation that was issued under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to be an official electronic version for the purposes of this Act (as if it were published under section 78).
-- src:1238 | 25 How power to issue official versions applies to previous or existing legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 25 (src:1238) (src:1239-1240)
GIVEN `the version was issued as an official electronic version under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the version continues to be an official electronic version` `the version was issued as an official electronic version under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012` MEANS
    `the version was issued as an official electronic version under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012`

-- src:1242 | Section 18(3) of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply to regulations or a legislative instrument (as defined in that Act) to which it applied immediately before the main commencement date.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 26 (src:1242)
GIVEN `it is regulations or a legislative instrument to which section 18(3) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied immediately before the main commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 18(3) of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply` `it is regulations or a legislative instrument to which section 18(3) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied immediately before the main commencement date` MEANS
    `it is regulations or a legislative instrument to which section 18(3) of the Legislation Act 2012 applied immediately before the main commencement date`

-- src:1244 | This clause applies to every copy of legislation—
-- src:1247 | Sections 16C and 16D of the Acts and Regulations Publication Act 1989 continue to apply to those copies despite the repeal of that Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 27 (src:1244-1247)
GIVEN `the copy purports to be printed and published under the authority of the New Zealand Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no official electronic or printed version has yet been issued under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012 or section 78` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sections 16C and 16D of the Acts and Regulations Publication Act 1989 continue to apply to the copy` `the copy purports to be printed and published under the authority of the New Zealand Government` `no official electronic or printed version has yet been issued under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012 or section 78` MEANS
    `the copy purports to be printed and published under the authority of the New Zealand Government` AND `no official electronic or printed version has yet been issued under section 17 of the Legislation Act 2012 or section 78`

-- src:1253 | Copies or reprints of legislation published under the Legislation Act 2012 must be taken never to have been required to include a statement that they are published under the authority of the New Zealand Government (despite section 6(6) of that Act).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 27B (src:1253)
GIVEN `the copy or reprint was published under the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the copy or reprint is taken to have been required to include a statement that it is published under the authority of the New Zealand Government` `the copy or reprint was published under the Legislation Act 2012` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1256 | Subpart 2 of Part 3 of this Act applies to legislation whether published by the PCO under this Act or any corresponding previous Acts.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 28 (src:1256)
GIVEN `the legislation was published by the PCO under this Act or any corresponding previous Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subpart 2 of Part 3 applies to the legislation` `the legislation was published by the PCO under this Act or any corresponding previous Acts` MEANS
    `the legislation was published by the PCO under this Act or any corresponding previous Acts`

-- src:1259 | References in this Act to a revision Bill or a revision Act (or a revision programme) include a Bill or an Act that is prepared (or a revision programme) under subpart 3 of Part 2 of the Legislation Act 2012.
-- src:1260 | References in this Act to sections 59 to 62 or subpart 3 of Part 3 of this Act include subpart 3 of Part 2 of the Legislation Act 2012.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 29 (src:1259-1260)
GIVEN `it is a Bill, an Act or a revision programme prepared under subpart 3 of Part 2 of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a revision Bill, a revision Act or a revision programme includes it` `it is a Bill, an Act or a revision programme prepared under subpart 3 of Part 2 of the Legislation Act 2012` MEANS
    `it is a Bill, an Act or a revision programme prepared under subpart 3 of Part 2 of the Legislation Act 2012`

-- 27A The first annual report required under section 83A must be provided to the Attorney-General as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year ending on 30 June 2022, and cover the period from the main commencement date to 30 June 2022.
-- "As soon as practicable" is an open-textured judgment and is taken as a plain input; the period the report covers is checked against the two dates.
-- src:1249 | The first annual report required under section 83A must—
-- src:1251 | cover the period from the main commencement date to 30 June 2022.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 27A (src:1249-1251)
GIVEN `it was provided to the Attorney-General as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year ending on 30 June 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period the report covers` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period the report covers` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first annual report meets clause 27A` `it was provided to the Attorney-General as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year ending on 30 June 2022` `the first day of the period the report covers` `the last day of the period the report covers` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` MEANS
        `it was provided to the Attorney-General as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year ending on 30 June 2022`
    AND (`the first day of the period the report covers` EQUALS `the main commencement date`)
    AND (`the last day of the period the report covers` EQUALS Date 30 6 2022)

§ `Schedule 1 clause 32 -- Limited application of presentation requirements to secondary legislation made before publication deadline`

-- src:1267 | This clause applies to secondary legislation that is made before the publication deadline for the secondary legislation.
-- src:1268 | Subpart 1 of Part 5 of this Act, which requires secondary legislation to be presented to the House of Representatives, applies to the secondary legislation only if—
-- src:1269 | it is made under an empowering provision that was enacted before the main commencement date and, before that date, instruments made under the provision were—
-- src:1270 | legislative instruments; or
-- src:1271 | instruments stated by an Act to be disallowable instruments for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012; or
-- src:1272 | expressly required to be presented to the House of Representatives; or
-- src:1273 | it is made under an empowering provision that was enacted on or after the main commencement date.
-- This clause applies to secondary legislation made before the publication deadline. Subpart 1 of Part 5 applies to it only if it is made under an empowering provision enacted before the main commencement date and, before that date, instruments made under the provision were legislative instruments, or
-- instruments stated by an Act to be disallowable, or expressly required to be presented; or it is made under an empowering provision enacted on or after the main commencement date. Outside the clause the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:1266 | 32 Limited application of presentation requirements to secondary legislation made before publication deadline
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 32(1) and (2) (src:1266) (src:1267-1273)
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE
      `the publication deadline` IS A DATE
      `the day the empowering provision was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
      `before that date, instruments made under the provision were legislative instruments, or stated by an Act to be disallowable instruments, or expressly required to be presented to the House` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`presentation to the House applies to the secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `before the publication deadline` `the publication deadline` `under a provision enacted on` `the day the empowering provision was enacted` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `where the earlier instruments were of the kinds listed:` `before that date, instruments made under the provision were legislative instruments, or stated by an Act to be disallowable instruments, or expressly required to be presented to the House` MEANS
    IF `the day the secondary legislation was made` LESS THAN `the publication deadline`
    THEN IF `the day the empowering provision was enacted` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`
         THEN JUST `before that date, instruments made under the provision were legislative instruments, or stated by an Act to be disallowable instruments, or expressly required to be presented to the House`
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) This clause does not affect any requirement for the legislation to be presented to the House of Representatives that applied when the secondary legislation was made.
-- src:1274 | This clause does not affect any requirement for the legislation to be presented to the House of Representatives that applied when the secondary legislation was made.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 32(3) (src:1274)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 32 affects a requirement for the legislation to be presented to the House that applied when it was made` MEANS FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 clauses 33, 33A and 34 -- Disallowance and confirmation transitions`

-- src:1277 | Subpart 1 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply to a notice of motion to disallow or amend a disallowable instrument (as defined in that Act) that is given, and not withdrawn or disposed of, before the main commencement date.
-- src:1276 | 33 Old disallowance provisions continue to apply to existing notices of motion, etc
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 33 (src:1276) (src:1277)
GIVEN `the day the notice of motion was given` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
      `it has been withdrawn or disposed of before the main commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subpart 1 of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply to the notice of motion given on` `the day the notice of motion was given` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `where it has been withdrawn or disposed of:` `it has been withdrawn or disposed of before the main commencement date` MEANS
    (`the day the notice of motion was given` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`) AND (NOT `it has been withdrawn or disposed of before the main commencement date`)

-- src:1279 | Subpart 2 of Part 5 of this Act (which provides for disallowance of secondary legislation), applies to anything that was an instrument of the following type at the time it was made (or an amendment to that instrument made at any time):
-- src:1281 | an instrument that was stated by an Act to be a disallowable instrument for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 33A (src:1279-1281)
GIVEN `it was a legislative instrument when made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act stated that it was not disallowable for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act stated that it was a disallowable instrument for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subpart 2 of Part 5 applies to the previously disallowable instrument` `it was a legislative instrument when made` `an Act stated that it was not disallowable for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012` `an Act stated that it was a disallowable instrument for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012` MEANS
    ((`it was a legislative instrument when made` AND (NOT `an Act stated that it was not disallowable for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012`)) OR `an Act stated that it was a disallowable instrument for the purposes of the Legislation Act 2012`)

-- src:1284 | Subpart 1A of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply to a confirmable instrument (as defined in section 47B of that Act) that was made before the main commencement date.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 1 clause 34 (src:1284)
GIVEN `it is a confirmable instrument as defined in section 47B of the Legislation Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subpart 1A of Part 3 of the Legislation Act 2012 continues to apply to the instrument` `it is a confirmable instrument as defined in section 47B of the Legislation Act 2012` `the day it was made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` MEANS
    `it is a confirmable instrument as defined in section 47B of the Legislation Act 2012` AND (`the day it was made` LESS THAN `the main commencement date`)

§ `Schedule 2 clause 1 -- Requirements to be met on proposal to incorporate material by reference`

-- src:1290 | 1 Requirements to be met on proposal to incorporate material by reference
-- src:1291 | Before secondary legislation incorporating material by reference in reliance on section 64 is made, the chief executive of the administering agency must—
-- src:1292 | give public notice of the proposal to incorporate the material, of the reasons for the proposal, and of how the material has been made publicly available; and
-- src:1293 | ensure that copies of the proposed material are publicly available in that way; and
-- src:1294 | allow a reasonable opportunity for persons to comment on the proposal; and
-- src:1295 | after considering any comments made and having regard to the purpose of this Act, be satisfied that—
-- src:1296 | the secondary legislation clearly identifies the material incorporated; and
-- src:1297 | the means of making the material publicly available is sufficient to enable persons to whom the law applies to find and obtain copies of the material incorporated with reasonable ease; and
-- src:1298 | it is otherwise appropriate to incorporate the proposed material as part of the secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 1 (src:1290) (src:1291-1298)
GIVEN `public notice has been given of the proposal, of the reasons for it, and of how the material has been made publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies of the proposed material are publicly available in that way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable opportunity to comment on the proposal has been allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive is satisfied that the secondary legislation clearly identifies the material incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive is satisfied that the means of making the material publicly available is sufficient for persons to find and obtain copies with reasonable ease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive is satisfied that it is otherwise appropriate to incorporate the proposed material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chief executive has met the requirements before the secondary legislation incorporating material is made` `public notice has been given of the proposal, of the reasons for it, and of how the material has been made publicly available` `copies of the proposed material are publicly available in that way` `a reasonable opportunity to comment on the proposal has been allowed` `the chief executive is satisfied that the secondary legislation clearly identifies the material incorporated` `the chief executive is satisfied that the means of making the material publicly available is sufficient for persons to find and obtain copies with reasonable ease` `the chief executive is satisfied that it is otherwise appropriate to incorporate the proposed material` MEANS
        `public notice has been given of the proposal, of the reasons for it, and of how the material has been made publicly available`
    AND `copies of the proposed material are publicly available in that way`
    AND `a reasonable opportunity to comment on the proposal has been allowed`
    AND `the chief executive is satisfied that the secondary legislation clearly identifies the material incorporated`
    AND `the chief executive is satisfied that the means of making the material publicly available is sufficient for persons to find and obtain copies with reasonable ease`
    AND `the chief executive is satisfied that it is otherwise appropriate to incorporate the proposed material`

§ `Schedule 2 clause 2 -- Access to material incorporated by reference`

-- src:1299 | 2 Access to material incorporated by reference
-- src:1300 | If an instrument incorporating material by reference in reliance on section 64 is made, the chief executive of the administering agency must—
-- src:1301 | give public notice of how the material is publicly available (or set this out in the secondary legislation); and
-- src:1302 | ensure that copies of the proposed material are publicly available in that way.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 2 (src:1299) (src:1300-1302)
GIVEN `public notice has been given of how the material is publicly available, or it is set out in the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies of the material are publicly available in that way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chief executive has met the requirements once the instrument incorporating material is made` `public notice has been given of how the material is publicly available, or it is set out in the secondary legislation` `copies of the material are publicly available in that way` MEANS
    `public notice has been given of how the material is publicly available, or it is set out in the secondary legislation` AND `copies of the material are publicly available in that way`

§ `Schedule 2 clause 3 -- What is required to make material publicly available`

-- src:1304 | A requirement to make material publicly available under this schedule is a requirement that—
-- src:1305 | the material is—
-- src:1306 | made available on (or via a link on) an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency, free of charge, unless doing so would infringe copyright; or
-- src:1307 | in any other case, available for inspection, free of charge, at a place notified on an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency; and
-- src:1308 | the material is available for purchase, at a reasonable cost, from a place notified on an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency; and
-- src:1309 | if the material is not in an official New Zealand language, an accurate translation in an official New Zealand language of the material is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b).
-- (1)(a) the material is (i) made available on (or via a link on) an Internet site maintained by or on behalf of the administering agency, free of charge, unless doing so would infringe copyright; or (ii) in any other case, available for inspection, free of charge, at a place notified on such an Internet site;
-- (b) the material is available for purchase, at a reasonable cost, from a place so notified; and (c) if the material is not in an official New Zealand language, an accurate translation is also available as set out in (a) and (b).
-- src:1303 | 3 What is required to make material publicly available
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 3(1) (src:1303) (src:1304-1309)
GIVEN `it is available on an Internet site of the administering agency, free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `doing so would infringe copyright` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is available for inspection free of charge at a place notified on such an Internet site` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is available for purchase at a reasonable cost from a place so notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in an official New Zealand language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an accurate translation is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the material is made publicly available as clause 3 requires` `it is available on an Internet site of the administering agency, free of charge` `doing so would infringe copyright` `it is available for inspection free of charge at a place notified on such an Internet site` `it is available for purchase at a reasonable cost from a place so notified` `it is in an official New Zealand language` `an accurate translation is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS
        (IF `doing so would infringe copyright` THEN `it is available for inspection free of charge at a place notified on such an Internet site` ELSE `it is available on an Internet site of the administering agency, free of charge`)
    AND `it is available for purchase at a reasonable cost from a place so notified`
    AND (`it is in an official New Zealand language` OR `an accurate translation is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b)`)

-- "An official New Zealand language" is used in paragraph (c) and defined nowhere in the Act (the languages that are official are fixed by other law, which the deposited sources do not include), so the Act answers NOTHING for every language (fork F15).
DECLARE `Language of the material` IS ONE OF
    English
    `te reo Māori`
    `New Zealand Sign Language`
    `another language`

-- src:1309 | if the material is not in an official New Zealand language, an accurate translation in an official New Zealand language of the material is also available as set out in paragraphs (a) and (b).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(c) (src:1309)
GIVEN language IS A `Language of the material`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an official New Zealand language` language MEANS
    CONSIDER language
    WHEN English THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `te reo Māori` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `New Zealand Sign Language` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `another language` THEN NOTHING

-- (2) A chief executive must not rely on section 66 of the Copyright Act 1994 as authority to make the proposed material available on an Internet site.
-- src:1310 | A chief executive must not rely on section 66 of the Copyright Act 1994 as authority to make the proposed material available on an Internet site.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 3(2) (src:1310)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a chief executive may rely on section 66 of the Copyright Act 1994 as authority to put the material on an Internet site` MEANS FALSE

§ `Schedule 2 clause 4 -- Proof of material incorporated by reference`

-- src:1312 | A copy of material incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64 must be—
-- src:1313 | certified as a correct copy of the material by the chief executive of the administering agency; and
-- src:1314 | retained by the chief executive.
-- src:1311 | 4 Proof of material incorporated by reference
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 4(1) (src:1311) (src:1312-1314)
GIVEN `a copy is certified as a correct copy by the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive retains it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the copy of the material has been certified and retained as clause 4 requires` `a copy is certified as a correct copy by the chief executive` `the chief executive retains it` MEANS
    `a copy is certified as a correct copy by the chief executive` AND `the chief executive retains it`

-- src:1315 | The production in a proceeding of a copy of the material incorporated by reference that is certified as a correct copy by the chief executive is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, sufficient evidence of the material incorporated by reference in the secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 4(2) (src:1315)
GIVEN `a copy certified as correct by the chief executive is produced in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certified copy is sufficient evidence of the material incorporated` `a copy certified as correct by the chief executive is produced in a proceeding` `there is evidence to the contrary` MEANS
    `a copy certified as correct by the chief executive is produced in a proceeding` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)

-- (3) See also Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which enables this requirement to be met by certifying and retaining a copy in an electronic form.
-- Whether that Part does so is a fact borrowed from that Act and is asked as an input.
-- src:1316 | See also Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which enables this requirement to be met by certifying and retaining a copy in an electronic form.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 4(3) (src:1316)
GIVEN `a copy has been certified as correct by the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been retained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in electronic form only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 enables the requirement to be met in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the requirement to certify and retain a copy is met` `a copy has been certified as correct by the chief executive` `it has been retained` `it is in electronic form only` `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 enables the requirement to be met in electronic form` MEANS
        `a copy has been certified as correct by the chief executive`
    AND `it has been retained`
    AND ((NOT `it is in electronic form only`) OR `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 enables the requirement to be met in electronic form`)

§ `Schedule 2 clauses 5 and 6 -- Publication, presentation and invalidity`

-- src:1318 | Subpart 1 of Part 3 and section 114 of this Act do not apply to material that is incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64 merely because it is incorporated.
-- src:1317 | 5 Material incorporated by reference need not be published under this Act or presented to House of Representatives
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 5 (src:1317) (src:1318)
GIVEN `it applies to the material merely because it is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subpart 1 of Part 3 and section 114 apply to the incorporated material` `it applies to the material merely because it is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1320 | A failure to comply with this schedule does not invalidate secondary legislation that incorporates material by reference.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 2 clause 6 (src:1320)
GIVEN `there is a failure to comply with Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a failure to comply with Schedule 2 invalidates the secondary legislation` `there is a failure to comply with Schedule 2` MEANS FALSE

§ `Schedule 3 -- Exemptions from presentation or disallowance (the opening rule)`

-- src:1322 | A presentation or disallowance exemption applies to secondary legislation (or part of secondary legislation) under this schedule if—
-- src:1323 | it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables below; and
-- src:1324 | any exemption ground is met (if specified in the tables for the exemption).
-- A presentation or disallowance exemption applies to secondary legislation (or part of it) under this schedule if it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables, and any exemption ground is met (if specified in the tables for the exemption).
-- The tables are shown only in part in the deposited text (the empowering provisions are missing from nearly every row): whether the provision is in the tables is an input.
-- src:1321 | Schedule 3 — Exemptions from presentation or disallowance under this Act
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 3 (src:1321) (src:1322-1324)
GIVEN `it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tables specify an exemption ground for the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption ground is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a presentation or disallowance exemption applies under Schedule 3` `it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables` `the tables specify an exemption ground for the exemption` `the exemption ground is met` MEANS
    `it is made under an empowering provision to which that exemption applies in accordance with the tables` AND ((NOT `the tables specify an exemption ground for the exemption`) OR `the exemption ground is met`)

-- 2 Any term or expression that is used in this schedule in relation to any empowering legislation has the meaning given to it in that legislation. The meaning is the empowering legislation's, so it is asked as an input.
-- src:1325 | Any term or expression that is used in this schedule in relation to any empowering legislation, but not defined in this Act, has the same meaning as in that empowering legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 3 (src:1325)
GIVEN `the term is used in Schedule 3 in relation to the empowering legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meaning the empowering legislation gives the term` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the meaning of a term used in Schedule 3` `the term is used in Schedule 3 in relation to the empowering legislation` `as given by the empowering legislation:` `the meaning the empowering legislation gives the term` MEANS
    IF `the term is used in Schedule 3 in relation to the empowering legislation` THEN `the meaning the empowering legislation gives the term` ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Exemption ground shown in the deposited text` IS ONE OF
    `Compliance is inappropriate for reasons of security`
    `Compliance would prejudice the national security interests of New Zealand`
    `The FMA is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance on the ground of commercial confidentiality`
    `The Takeovers Panel is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance for reasons of commercial confidentiality`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information, disclosure of a trade secret, prejudice to New Zealand's position in negotiations for overseas market access, or prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of commercially sensitive information`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in disclosure of a trade secret`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in prejudice to New Zealand's position in current or future negotiations for overseas market access`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in prejudice to New Zealand's position in current negotiations for overseas market access`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in prejudice to New Zealand's position in future negotiations for overseas market access`
    `The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand`
    `The secondary legislation is bylaws made under the regulations for the purposes of section 49 of Ngā Rohe Moana o Ngā Hapū o Ngāti Porou Act 2019`

-- Whether each ground continues once met differs: most say "Exemption applies if exemption ground is met"; one (the Takeovers Panel row) says "Exemption applies while exemption ground is met". The table's other columns are lost, so this encodes the ground only.
-- src:1330 | Compliance is inappropriate for reasons of security.
-- src:1345 | Compliance would prejudice the national security interests of New Zealand.
-- src:1363 | If the FMA is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance on the ground of commercial confidentiality.
-- src:1367 | The secondary legislation is bylaws made under the regulations for the purposes of section 49 of Ngā Rohe Moana o Ngā Hapū o Ngāti Porou Act 2019.
-- src:1380 | The relevant chief executive considers that compliance would result in 1 or more of the following:
-- src:1381 | disclosure of commercially sensitive information:
-- src:1382 | disclosure of a trade secret:
-- src:1383 | prejudice to New Zealand’s position in current or future negotiations for overseas market access:
-- src:1384 | prejudice to the international relations of New Zealand.
-- src:1405 | The Takeovers Panel is satisfied on reasonable grounds that it is proper to defer compliance for reasons of commercial confidentiality.
-- src:1406 | Exemption applies while exemption ground is met
@ref Legislation Act 2019 Schedule 3, exemption grounds (src:1330) (src:1345) (src:1363) (src:1367) (src:1380-1384) (src:1405-1406)
GIVEN ground IS AN `Exemption ground shown in the deposited text`
      `the condition the ground states is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exemption ground is met in the way the deposited text shows` ground `when` `the condition the ground states is met` MEANS
    `the condition the ground states is met`
